#!/bin/sh
# Project-specific pre-push guards — a MENU OF SHAPES to copy FROM.
#
# APPEND what you need to the bottom of .githooks/pre-push-project. Do NOT copy
# this file over it: `pre-push-project` ships already populated, wiring the
# regression suites that guard the blueprint-managed machinery your project runs
# (blueprint pull/drift/a2bp, signal-set.sh, the feed, the hooks, the gate
# renderer). Overwriting it takes all of them off your push path in one command,
# and the gate keeps printing PASSED over the remainder — which is BUG-004 and
# A-22 exactly, so it would not look like a mistake (BUG-028).
#
# It is excluded from blueprint sync on purpose: your project owns the bottom of
# it, so `blueprint pull` must never overwrite it.
#
# Examples (uncomment and adapt):

